hias</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>A graphical assessment of <italic>p</italic>-values from sliding window haplotype tests of association to identify asthma susceptibility loci on chromosome 11q.</article-title><source>BMC Genetics</source><volume>7</volume><fpage>38</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16774684</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003746-Andolfatto1"><label>33</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Andolfatto</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Unusual haplotype structure at the proximal breakpoint of In(2L)t in a natural population of Drosophila melanogaster.</article-title><source>Genetics</source><volume>153</volume><fpage>1297</fpage><lpage>1311</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10545460</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003746-Tajima1"><label>34</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tajima</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><year>1991</year><article-title>Determination of window size for analyzing DNA sequences.</article-title><source>J Mol Evol</source><volume>33</volume><fpage>470</fpage><lpage>473</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1960744</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003746-Ardell1"><label>35</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ardell</surname><given-names>DH</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>SCANMS: Adjusting for multiple comparisons in sliding window neutrality tests.</article-title><source>Bioinformatics</source><volume>20</volume><fpage>1986</fpage><lpage>1988</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15059827</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003746-Talbert1"><label>36</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Talbert</surname><given-names>PB</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Adaptive evolution of centromere proteins in plants and animals.</article-title><source>J Biol</source><volume>3</volume><fpage>18</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15345035</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003746-Nielsen1"><label>37</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nielsen</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Likelihood models for detecting positively selected amino acid sites and applications to the HIV-1 envelope gene.</article-title><source>Genetics</source><volume>148</volume><fpage>929</fpage><lpage>936</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9539414</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003746-Yang6"><label>38</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yang</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Codon-substitution models for heterogeneous selection pressure at amino acid sites.</article-title><source>Genetics</source><volume>155</volume><fpage>431</fpage><lpage>449</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10790415</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003746-Self1"><label>39</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Self</surname><given-names>SG</given-names></name></person-group><year>1987</year><article-title>Asymptotic properties of maximum likelihood estimators and likelihood ratio tests under nonstandard conditions.</article-title><source>J Am Stat Assoc</source><volume>82</volume><fpage>605</fpage><lpage>610</lpage></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn fn-type="conflict"><p><bold>Competing Interests: </bold>The authors have declared that no competing interests exist.</p></fn><fn fn-type="financial-disclosure"><p><bold>Funding: </bold>The authors have no support or funding to report.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>